## 5. Sequential CLI Execution Plan

Follow this exact sequence when instructing the CLI agent to build out the editor modules:

### Prompt 01: Assembly & Grouping Engine

> Implement `scripts/editor/grouping/assembly_root.gd` and `assembly_serializer.gd`. Support multi-selection bundling via `Ctrl + G` into an `AssemblyRoot3D` node, centering the root origin to the selection's aggregate `AABB`. Implement `Ctrl + Shift + G` to disband assemblies while keeping global transforms intact. Add export/import of assemblies to `user://prefabs/[name].json`.

### Prompt 02: VFX Definition & Emitter Subsystem

> Implement `scripts/editor/effects/vfx_definition.gd` as an `@export` Resource. Create `scripts/editor/effects/vfx_registry.gd` to autoload and scan `res://resources/vfx/`. Create `scripts/editor/effects/effect_emitter_3d.gd` as a placeable editor entity that instances the configured particle scene and audio stream upon receiving a trigger, with an optional radial overlap query applying damage and impulse to nearby actors.

### Prompt 03: Runtime Asset Ingestion

> Implement `scripts/editor/ingestion/asset_importer.gd`, `mesh_loader.gd`, `texture_loader.gd`, and `audio_loader.gd`. Utilize `GLTFDocument` to load `.glb`/`.gltf` files from `user://custom_assets/meshes/` with dynamic convex collision hulls. Ingest `.png` images into `ImageTexture` resources for decals, and stream `.ogg`/`.wav` audio tracks for in-world playback without requiring Godot editor recompilation.

### Prompt 04: Visual Logic Nodes & Event Graph

> Implement `scripts/editor/events/logic_node_base.gd` and the node library (`trigger_volume.gd`, `door_actuator.gd`, `radio_transmitter.gd`, `orta_tracker.gd`). Implement `scripts/editor/events/event_manager.gd` to parse the map's `event_graph` on level start and dynamically connect output signals to target callables via `source.connect(signal_name, Callable(target, action))`.

### Prompt 05: Viewport Wire Spline Renderer

> Implement `scripts/editor/events/logic_wire_renderer.gd`. When the user is in "Linker / Wiring Mode", render 3D line splines using `ImmediateMesh` between connected logic nodes in the editor viewport. Ensure the splines update in real time if linked nodes are translated or rotated.

### Prompt 06: Dynamic NavMesh Baking Integration

> Update the level editor controller to support runtime navigation re-baking. Hook a UI button to `NavigationRegion3D.bake_navigation_mesh()`, ensuring user-placed geometry and custom meshes are correctly parsed on the collision mask so enemy bots and New Ottoman infantry can pathfind over user-created layouts.

